  "sandbox_disclosure": "D-352 (5), as D-346 (3): at c220781, before the A3 code was reviewed, a node sandbox computed A3-top for llama31 at 200 draws (anchor-only: 4d B's A1 values, reproduced bit for bit) and the predictions plus the full simulation for llama31 at 5 draws; nobody read their A3-benign, A3-band or P-A3.x fields; this record is written fresh by the reviewed code, and no sandbox figure is quoted",
  "prediction_function": {
    "module": "src/phase3_a3_predictions.py",
    "function": "predicted_tpr",
    "formula": "predicted TPR = F1bar(t'), t' = the k-th largest of the clean pool's post scores together with the m injected items' post scores, k = floor(alpha * (n + m)), alpha = 0.01; F1bar(t) = share of eval positives with post score >= t; per draw and seed (D-332 P-A3.1)",
    "sha256": "7e22451a5f25fbd2ded673911d413ea24d421222c01fa91fbae7c63dbd179ccc",
    "threshold": "kth_largest(clean pool + injected post scores, whole_item_k)"
  },
  "order": "computes no repair on a poisoned pool (t' is the stated order statistic by np.sort, not paired.thr_at_fpr, quantile_transfer or restandardisation); written before this pair's simulation, which refuses without it (D-332 (5), (7))",
  "implementation_choices": {
    "a": "probe set: the selected C only (D-332 (1); D-346 (2)(a))",
    "b": "P-A3.1 cells: pair x pool x attacker x rho with the pool's score-level repair (threshold re-set on R_same and R_fresh, quantile transfer on traffic); restandardisation is not predicted by P-A3.1 (its threshold is T_d on restandardised scores, not an order statistic; D-221 P4) and is scored by P-A3.4 (D-332 (5)). On the 32 threshold re-set cells of 48 (about two thirds) the prediction is the repair's own rule on the same pool, so they agree by construction up to ties at the k-th place. D-332's 1% rule is not quantile transfer's rule on traffic: the transfer carries the clean pre window's tail share at T_d (its harmful items included) to the poisoned post window, so its threshold sits below t' and the traffic cells are expected to be under-predicted",
    "c": "F1bar(t) = share of eval positives with post score >= t, the project's flag rule (paired.thr_at_fpr's exceedance; D-221's notation)",
    "d": "k = int(math.floor(alpha * (n + m))) (equal to the largest c with c/(n+m) <= alpha on the grid, tested); the k-th largest counts ties with multiplicity (np.sort(x)[N - k]) (D-242: whole items)",
    "e": "A3-benign ranked by the seed-mean post score with 4d B's A1 expression np.argsort(-mean) (D-244 (4))",
    "f": "A3-benign candidates: every probe_train negative, as D-332 (3) names them; each seed's fit rows are among them (F-060, D-221). A confound with a direction (D-352 (2), rule 5): the fit rows are 80% of probe_train (D-117's 20% hold-out aside), so about 80% of the candidates are, per seed, that seed's own fit rows, which score low under the probe fitted on them (why F-045 / F-060 keep fit rows out of every 4d pool); this weakens A3-benign and biases P-A3.2 toward holding. The realised share among the injected items is recorded per seed (benign_fit_row_share_per_seed)",
    "g": "a cell's prediction is the D-156 mean over the 200 draws of the per-draw mean over seeds, frozen split beside (D-156; D-346 (4))",
    "h": "the injections (first round(0.25 n) items per pool and draw for A3-top, per pair for A3-benign) are stored in the npz and bound bit for bit by the simulation"
  },
